      "explanation": "His sudden flank-to-groin pain, inability to lie still and haematuria suggest ureteric colic. Non-contrast CT is the appropriate definitive imaging study in this non-pregnant adult and can show a stone, its location and obstruction. IV contrast is not needed to identify the calculus.",
