      "confidence": "supported",
      "basis": "lecture",
      "explanation": "A collapsed lobe often becomes a linear or wedge-shaped opacity that points toward the hilum. Its defining feature is volume loss, which can pull the hilum, fissures and mediastinum toward it; uncomplicated pneumonia usually preserves volume.",
