      "explanation": "CT urography has largely replaced IV urography for detailed urinary-tract assessment. Its cross-sectional images evaluate the kidneys and surrounding tissues, while delayed contrast images show the collecting systems and ureters. This contrast study is different from the non-contrast CT used primarily for stones.",
